NO LICENCE IS GRANTED AT THIS TIME.

This repository is source-available, not open source. The code is published so
that people can read it, run it on their own eclipse data, and tell me where it
breaks. A proper licence will follow once it is clear what the project should
be; until then the default of copyright law applies and the paragraphs below say
plainly what I do and do not intend by that.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

Because this repository is public on GitHub, GitHub's Terms of Service already
let you view it and fork it within GitHub. Beyond that, and for the avoidance of
doubt:

  * Run it on your own images, for any purpose, commercial or not.
  * Modify your own copy to make it work with your data.
  * Open issues and pull requests.

THE IMAGES YOU MAKE WITH IT ARE ENTIRELY YOURS.

This is worth stating on its own line, because non-commercial software licences
often leave it ambiguous. I claim nothing over anything you photograph, process
or produce with this tool: no rights, no royalty, no attribution requirement.
Sell the prints, license the images, publish them, put them in a book. That the
software is restricted does not reach through to your pictures.


WHAT IS NOT GRANTED

Redistributing the code outside GitHub, publishing modified versions, bundling
it into another product, selling it, or offering it as a service. None of that
is permitted at present. If you want to do any of it, ask — the answer is likely
to be yes with conditions, and a request is what will tell me which licence this
project actually needs.


WHERE THIS IS HEADED

The intent is that people should be free to use and improve this without paying
for it, that nobody should be able to sell it or close it off, and that
improvements should stay available under the same terms. No widely used software
licence expresses exactly that combination, so rather than pick a poor fit in a
hurry, this stays unlicensed while the question is open. Suggestions welcome in
an issue.


CONTRIBUTIONS

By opening a pull request you agree that your contribution may be included in
this project and released under whatever licence the project eventually adopts,
alongside the rest of the code.


